/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A system is any rule, device or process that acts on an input signal and produces an output signal.
   - The label CT or DT comes from the independent variable of the signals, not from the hardware.
   - A computer can simulate a CT model by taking small time steps.
   - Large systems are built from smaller blocks.
   - The DT forms are identical with square brackets: y[n]=T₂{T₁{x[n]}} for series, and y[n]=T₁{x[n]}+T₂{x[n]} for parallel.
   - An audio chain is a series connection: microphone, equaliser, amplifier, speaker.
   - When blocks are linear and time-invariant, let h₁(t) and h₂(t) be their impulse responses.
   - Classification answers practical questions before any calculation.
   - The formal tests for linearity, time invariance, causality and stability are in Chapter 1.6.
   - To classify a system from its equation, ask three questions in order.
*/
