/* book exam traps: CT and DT describe the independent variable. A digital computer that simulates a CT model does not make the model DT. | Causal is not the same as memoryless. y[n]=x[n−1] is causal but has memory; y[n]=x[n+1] is noncausal. | A constant term breaks linearity. y(t)=3x(t)+2 is nonlinear and time-invariant, not linear. | Stability and time invariance are independent. A system can be time-invariant and unstable, for example y[n]=2y[n−1]+x[n], a recursive system whose feedback gain 2 doubles the output every step: for x[n] = δ[n] it gives y[n] = 2ⁿu[n], which grows without bound | Squaring is not a small detail: y[n]=x[n]² is nonlinear over real inputs and not invertible, because x and −x give the same output. */
